{:edb/db-before-t 2449 :edb/db-after-t 2450 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535762 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:43:40.610Z" 13194139535762 true] [17592186179665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365144 13194139535762 true] [17592186179665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365151 13194139535762 true] [17592186179666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365130 13194139535762 true] [17592186179666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365137 13194139535762 true] [17592186179667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365123 13194139535762 true] [17592186365123 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365124 13194139535762 true] [17592186365123 1089 "q-125047" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365123 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535762 true] [17592186365123 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\sqrt{xy}\\,j$ and $C$ is the line segment traversed from the point $A(1,1)$ to the point $B(4,3)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(1+3t)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j.$*" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365123 1113 #uuid "4b9560c5-3975-50c2-be49-907f5e986e32" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365123 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the line segment.\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are \n$a=i+j$ and $b=4\\,i+3\\,j.$\nSo, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =(i+j)+t[(4\\,i+3\\,j)-(i+j)] \\\\  & =(i+j)+t(3i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =(1+3t)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ varies from $t=0$ (at the point $A$) to $t=1$ (at the point $B$).\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=1+3t,\\,y=1+2t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\sqrt{xy}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3t+1+2t)\\,i+\\sqrt{(1+3t)(1+2t)}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,j)\\cdot (3\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\cdot 3+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365125 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365126 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365127 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365128 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365129 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1041 "selection" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365127 13194139535762 true] [17592186365124 1110 #uuid "53fd0561-0984-5a0c-9670-b6fbf2e18e94" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365125 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365125 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365125 1111 #uuid "bfb0d7ea-99d3-50ad-afe3-952dc466428f" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365126 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t)+6\\sqrt{6}t\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365126 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365126 1111 #uuid "9f9e1606-58a8-557c-a6e3-49f73c5ac643" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365127 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365127 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365127 1111 #uuid "2790fdbf-9539-5028-88d3-888079a9cf3b" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365128 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+6\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365128 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365128 1111 #uuid "c9f8ed32-ffa6-55b3-997a-c24b86aeca91" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365129 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t)+3\\sqrt{6}t\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365129 1111 #uuid "d6c931df-1f47-523e-80a7-96ae3668f44f" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365130 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365131 13194139535762 true] [17592186365130 1089 "q-125065" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365130 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535762 true] [17592186365130 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i+2y\\,j$ and $C$ is the curve $\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-x=0$ traversed from the point $A(0,1)$ to the point $B(1,e).$" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365130 1113 #uuid "93eab229-7847-5466-9349-e69354e42020" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365130 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Making $x$ the subject of the equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-x=0\\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.\n$$\n\nSo, the parametrization of the curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j,\\,1\\le t\\le e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+2y\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+2t\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}+2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡t}{2}+{t}^{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}+{e}^{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365132 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365133 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365134 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365135 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365136 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1041 "selection" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365136 13194139535762 true] [17592186365131 1110 #uuid "ef7f9e25-d9ec-5d72-885f-ed71ee3ac6b1" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365132 1034 "e-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365132 1111 #uuid "4678d7e5-82b8-5e87-9c6b-b5dfd48f83e4" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365133 1034 "{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365133 1111 #uuid "ed46e1fc-ec22-5349-8a9c-98856b673a11" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365134 1034 "e+\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365134 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365134 1111 #uuid "c8ee05bc-92ff-58be-9189-349e4480ad7e" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365135 1034 "\\frac{e-1}{2}" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365135 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365135 1111 #uuid "7bd3f11d-30ad-53f8-8d47-b51f76d658f5" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365136 1034 "{e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365136 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365136 1111 #uuid "06237856-dba3-5602-a1ea-9cb2e60c7ec4" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365137 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365138 13194139535762 true] [17592186365137 1089 "q-125119" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365137 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535762 true] [17592186365137 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=2y\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j$ and $C$ is the curve $\\sqrt{y}=x+3$ traversed from the point $A(-3,0)$ to the point $B(-1,4)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(\\sqrt{t}-3)\\,i+t\\,j.$*" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365137 1113 #uuid "df07dcc3-786b-5aae-b240-3c57fcb3d038" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365137 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. This is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(\\sqrt{t}-3)\\,i+t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{t}-3,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2t\\,i+(\\sqrt{t}-3)^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+(t-6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}-3)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2t\\,i+(t-6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =2t\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+t-6\\sqrt{t}+9 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{t}+t-6\\sqrt{t}+9 \\\\  & =t-5\\sqrt{t}+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-5\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365139 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365140 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365141 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365142 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365143 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1041 "selection" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365142 13194139535762 true] [17592186365138 1110 #uuid "09db5dcb-67ae-5125-ba36-290effd28794" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365139 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t+6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365139 1111 #uuid "f63f7263-d177-53f7-b86d-89ddbfcd5fbd" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365140 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t+5\\sqrt{t}+3)\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365140 1111 #uuid "4cc3892f-9f03-50d7-b490-58aeb2789c71" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365141 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-4\\sqrt{t}+3)\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365141 1111 #uuid "1658e889-2720-538f-91da-00561f458388" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365142 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-5\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365142 1111 #uuid "a436f2bb-1a72-5a83-a377-98dfba9a9f4b" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365143 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365143 1111 #uuid "a8ae2d93-ee15-5bd6-948f-30d522d0fad2" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365144 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365145 13194139535762 true] [17592186365144 1089 "q-77008" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365144 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535762 true] [17592186365144 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/assets/dea7eed9213ddf1bb3293950e2490b120a061e9add1172d3b850ccbc58f90454.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(y+x)\\,i+x\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4$ traversed from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $B(0,-1).$" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365144 1113 #uuid "86093429-bf79-5738-9f65-4a1d67949670" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365144 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Notice that we can write its equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, our curve is a part-ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $2$ and $1$ respectively. This curve can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(y+x)\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =((\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2(-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,dt \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-1+0]-[1-0] \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365146 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365147 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365148 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365149 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365150 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1041 "selection" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365150 13194139535762 true] [17592186365145 1110 #uuid "54a45544-c0aa-50c0-90ce-418e9cc6f417" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365146 1034 "\\pi -2" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365146 1111 #uuid "09fe2727-a04c-5f16-b597-7e39f4e3b962" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365147 1034 "2-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365147 1111 #uuid "17c17ee5-e87e-5d33-bfd3-5f9e8b91d0db" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365148 1034 "2" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365148 1111 #uuid "4b97a787-a1f0-54f9-8bad-14b138fe3430" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365149 1034 "0" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365149 1111 #uuid "f471322e-f88e-5279-987d-5a0721866964" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365150 1034 "-2" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365150 1111 #uuid "b4aacb1a-8ca5-547f-9995-cf3baa6e0fd9" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365151 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365152 13194139535762 true] [17592186365151 1089 "q-77032" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365151 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535762 true] [17592186365151 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/assets/08c3195e7325d853f61562b1f62460cb0796f14377286228f2b7cd40983202ac.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=3\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16$  traversed from the point $A(4,0)$ to the point $B(0,4).$" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365151 1113 #uuid "04f1da30-9079-5727-a65a-17c34fc10145" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365151 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize a circle of radius $4$ centered at the origin. It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =3\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =3\\,i+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(3\\,i+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)\\,dt \\\\  & =[12\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(12+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365153 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365154 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365155 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365156 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365157 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1041 "selection" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365156 13194139535762 true] [17592186365152 1110 #uuid "7b92ea35-3cdf-505b-9c80-09274ed9f682" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365153 1034 "\\pi -12" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365153 1111 #uuid "a441d62a-dd57-5be0-9906-7cbcea70660e" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365154 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535762 true] [17592186365154 1111 #uuid "f5a477cc-69e4-5469-b8db-19bbe69f353f" 13194139535762 true] [17592186365155 1034 "12-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 1319